{"parentUuid":"5e0cc8c0-36ef-4565-ac4f-f6631b00b3ee","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"6d252faa-d8a9-475a-b3d8-d0489bc8da88","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"floofy-puzzling-candle","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01JhMC2bHy4CkYnJ5B26sMZy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create the skill documents:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":43539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbCPpdpSvFwGG1joVkoS","type":"assistant","uuid":"47fc562c-b2b9-4049-96a3-868b26c2f4db","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:29:22.779Z"}
{"parentUuid":"47fc562c-b2b9-4049-96a3-868b26c2f4db","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"6d252faa-d8a9-475a-b3d8-d0489bc8da88","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"floofy-puzzling-candle","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01JhMC2bHy4CkYnJ5B26sMZy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GActXg8AwbXbPDGZfwFx8U","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/pandas-excel-processing.md","content":"# Pandas Excel File Processing\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers reading, processing, and analyzing Excel files (.xlsx, .xls) using pandas, a powerful data manipulation library in Python.\n\n## Installation\n```bash\npip install pandas openpyxl\n```\n\n- `pandas`: Core data manipulation library\n- `openpyxl`: Required for reading/writing Excel 2010+ files (.xlsx)\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### Reading Excel Files\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Read entire Excel file (first sheet by default)\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx')\n\n# Read specific sheet by name\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', sheet_name='Sheet1')\n\n# Read specific sheet by index (0-based)\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', sheet_name=0)\n\n# Read all sheets\nall_sheets = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', sheet_name=None)\n```\n\n### Common DataFrame Operations\n```python\n# View first/last rows\nprint(df.head())      # First 5 rows\nprint(df.tail(10))    # Last 10 rows\n\n# Get DataFrame info\nprint(df.shape)       # (rows, columns)\nprint(df.columns)     # Column names\nprint(df.dtypes)      # Data types\n\n# Access columns\ncolumn_data = df['ColumnName']\nmultiple_cols = df[['Col1', 'Col2']]\n\n# Access rows by index\nrow = df.iloc[0]      # First row\nrows = df.iloc[0:5]   # First 5 rows\n\n# Filter data\nfiltered = df[df['Score'] > 50]\nfiltered = df[df['Name'] == 'Player1']\n\n# Get unique values\nunique_values = df['ColumnName'].unique()\n\n# Count values\nvalue_counts = df['ColumnName'].value_counts()\n```\n\n### Handling Large Files\n```python\n# Read only specific columns\ndf = pd.read_excel('large_file.xlsx', usecols=['Col1', 'Col2'])\n\n# Read with data types specification\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', dtype={'GameID': int, 'Score': float})\n\n# Skip rows\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', skiprows=5)\n\n# Limit rows\ndf = pd.read_excel('data.xlsx', nrows=1000)\n```\n\n## Data Analysis Examples\n\n### Basic Statistics\n```python\n# Summary statistics\nprint(df.describe())\n\n# Mean, median, sum\nmean_score = df['Score'].mean()\nmedian_score = df['Score'].median()\ntotal_score = df['Score'].sum()\n\n# Count non-null values\ncount = df['ColumnName'].count()\n```\n\n### Grouping and Aggregation\n```python\n# Group by column and calculate statistics\ngrouped = df.groupby('Player')['Score'].sum()\ngrouped = df.groupby('Player').agg({'Score': ['sum', 'mean', 'count']})\n\n# Multiple grouping\ngrouped = df.groupby(['Player', 'GameType'])['Score'].mean()\n```\n\n### Sorting and Ranking\n```python\n# Sort by column\ndf_sorted = df.sort_values('Score', ascending=False)\n\n# Sort by multiple columns\ndf_sorted = df.sort_values(['Player', 'Score'], ascending=[True, False])\n```\n\n## Common Patterns for Game Data Analysis\n\n### Comparing Two Players\n```python\n# Separate data by player\nplayer1_data = df[df['PlayerID'] == 1]\nplayer2_data = df[df['PlayerID'] == 2]\n\n# Compare statistics\np1_wins = len(player1_data[player1_data['Result'] == 'Win'])\np2_wins = len(player2_data[player2_data['Result'] == 'Win'])\n\n# Match-based comparison (pairing rows)\nfor i in range(0, len(df), 2):\n    game1 = df.iloc[i]\n    game2 = df.iloc[i+1]\n    # Compare game1 vs game2\n```\n\n### Working with Game Numbers\n```python\n# Filter odd/even numbered games\nodd_games = df[df['GameNumber'] % 2 == 1]\neven_games = df[df['GameNumber'] % 2 == 0]\n\n# Add game number if not present\ndf['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n```\n\n## Performance Tips\n1. Use `usecols` to read only needed columns for large files\n2. Specify `dtype` to avoid automatic type inference\n3. Use `nrows` for testing with large datasets\n4. Consider using `pd.read_excel(..., engine='openpyxl')` for better compatibility\n\n## Common Errors and Solutions\n\n### Error: \"XLRDError: Excel xlsx file; not supported\"\n**Solution**: Install openpyxl: `pip install openpyxl`\n\n### Error: \"Memory Error with large files\"\n**Solution**: Read in chunks or use `usecols` and `nrows` to limit data\n\n### Error: \"KeyError: 'ColumnName'\"\n**Solution**: Check column names with `df.columns`, they may have leading/trailing spaces\n\n## References\n- [Pandas Documentation](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/)\n- [Pandas Excel I/O](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/io.html#excel-files)\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":247,"cache_read_input_tokens":43539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":247,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbCPpdpSvFwGG1joVkoS","type":"assistant","uuid":"e7c27796-a5b5-4b7f-8699-60dfdd5eae25","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:29:41.607Z"}
