number if not present\ndf['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n```\n\n## Performance Tips\n1. Use `usecols` to read only needed columns for large files\n2. Specify `dtype` to avoid automatic type inference\n3. Use `nrows` for testing with large datasets\n4. Consider using `pd.read_excel(..., engine='openpyxl')` for better compatibility\n\n## Common Errors and Solutions\n\n### Error: \"XLRDError: Excel xlsx file; not supported\"\n**Solution**: Install openpyxl: `pip install openpyxl`\n\n### Error: \"Memory Error with large files\"\n**Solution**: Read in chunks or use `usecols` and `nrows` to limit data\n\n### Error: \"KeyError: 'ColumnName'\"\n**Solution**: Check column names with `df.columns`, they may have leading/trailing spaces\n\n## References\n- [Pandas Documentation](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/)\n- [Pandas Excel I/O](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/io.html#excel-files)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7c27796-a5b5-4b7f-8699-60dfdd5eae25"}
{"parentUuid":"de1931cf-c9f0-49ac-9856-55398cf1e0c3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"6d252faa-d8a9-475a-b3d8-d0489bc8da88","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"floofy-puzzling-candle","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_017N21RwDzDR8GTDoANCG9se","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AevvXUiEVBtMTgTKLia4N9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/python-pdf-reading.md","content":"# Python PDF Reading\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers reading and extracting text from PDF files using Python libraries. There are several approaches depending on the PDF structure.\n\n## Available Libraries\n\n### 1. PyPDF2\nBasic PDF reading, good for simple text extraction.\n\n**Installation:**\n```bash\npip install PyPDF2\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\n# Open PDF file\nwith open('document.pdf', 'rb') as file:\n    pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n\n    # Get number of pages\n    num_pages = len(pdf_reader.pages)\n\n    # Extract text from specific page\n    page = pdf_reader.pages[0]\n    text = page.extract_text()\n\n    # Extract from all pages\n    full_text = ''\n    for page_num in range(num_pages):\n        page = pdf_reader.pages[page_num]\n        full_text += page.extract_text()\n```\n\n### 2. pdfplumber\nMore advanced, better for tables and structured data.\n\n**Installation:**\n```bash\npip install pdfplumber\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\n# Open PDF\nwith pdfplumber.open('document.pdf') as pdf:\n    # Get first page\n    first_page = pdf.pages[0]\n\n    # Extract text\n    text = first_page.extract_text()\n\n    # Extract tables\n    tables = first_page.extract_tables()\n\n    # Extract from all pages\n    full_text = ''\n    for page in pdf.pages:\n        full_text += page.extract_text()\n```\n\n### 3. pymupdf (fitz)\nFast and powerful, good for complex PDFs.\n\n**Installation:**\n```bash\npip install pymupdf\n```\n\n**Usage:**\n```python\nimport fitz  # PyMuPDF\n\n# Open PDF\npdf_document = fitz.open('document.pdf')\n\n# Iterate through pages\nfor page_num in range(pdf_document.page_count):\n    page = pdf_document[page_num]\n    text = page.get_text()\n    print(text)\n\npdf_document.close()\n```\n\n## Common Use Cases\n\n### Extract All Text from PDF\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\ndef extract_all_text(pdf_path):\n    with open(pdf_path, 'rb') as file:\n        pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n        text = ''\n        for page in pdf_reader.pages:\n            text += page.extract_text() + '\\n'\n    return text\n\n# Usage\nfull_text = extract_all_text('document.pdf')\nprint(full_text)\n```\n\n### Extract Specific Pages\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\ndef extract_page_range(pdf_path, start_page, end_page):\n    with open(pdf_path, 'rb') as file:\n        pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n        text = ''\n        for page_num in range(start_page, min(end_page + 1, len(pdf_reader.pages))):\n            text += pdf_reader.pages[page_num].extract_text() + '\\n'\n    return text\n\n# Extract pages 1-5 (0-indexed)\ntext = extract_page_range('document.pdf', 0, 4)\n```\n\n### Search for Keywords\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\ndef search_pdf(pdf_path, keyword):\n    results = []\n    with open(pdf_path, 'rb') as file:\n        pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n        for page_num, page in enumerate(pdf_reader.pages):\n            text = page.extract_text()\n            if keyword.lower() in text.lower():\n                results.append({\n                    'page': page_num + 1,\n                    'text_snippet': text[:200]\n                })\n    return results\n\n# Find all pages containing \"Player\"\nmatches = search_pdf('document.pdf', 'Player')\n```\n\n### Extract Tables from PDF\n```python\nimport pdfplumber\n\ndef extract_tables(pdf_path):\n    tables = []\n    with pdfplumber.open(pdf_path) as pdf:\n        for page in pdf.pages:\n            page_tables = page.extract_tables()\n            tables.extend(page_tables)\n    return tables\n\n# Usage\nall_tables = extract_tables('document.pdf')\nfor i, table in enumerate(all_tables):\n    print(f\"Table {i+1}:\")\n    for row in table:\n        print(row)\n```\n\n## Handling Large PDFs\n\n### Read First Few Pages Only\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\ndef read_first_n_pages(pdf_path, n=5):\n    with open(pdf_path, 'rb') as file:\n        pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n        text = ''\n        for page_num in range(min(n, len(pdf_reader.pages))):\n            text += pdf_reader.pages[page_num].extract_text() + '\\n'\n    return text\n\n# Read first 10 pages\nsample_text = read_first_n_pages('large_document.pdf', 10)\n```\n\n### Extract Metadata\n```python\nimport PyPDF2\n\ndef get_pdf_metadata(pdf_path):\n    with open(pdf_path, 'rb') as file:\n        pdf_reader = PyPDF2.PdfReader(file)\n        metadata = pdf_reader.metadata\n        info = {\n            'pages': len(pdf_reader.pages),\n            'author': metadata.get('/Author', 'Unknown'),\n            'title': metadata.get('/Title', 'Unknown'),\n            'subject': metadata.get('/Subject', 'Unknown'),\n            'creator': metadata.get('/Creator', 'Unknown')\n        }\n    return info\n```\n\n## Common Issues and Solutions\n\n### Issue: Extracted text is garbled or empty\n**Possible causes:**\n- PDF is image-based (scanned document) - need OCR\n- PDF has complex formatting\n- Text is embedded as images\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Try different libraries (pdfplumber, pymupdf)\n2. Use OCR libraries like `pytesseract` for scanned PDFs\n3. Check if PDF is encrypted\n\n### Issue: \"PdfReadError: EOF marker not found\"\n**Solution:** PDF file may be corrupted or incomplete. Try opening with different library.\n\n### Issue: Memory error with large PDFs\n**Solution:** Process pages one at a time instead of loading entire document.\n\n```python\n# Process page by page\nimport PyPDF2\n\nwith open('large.pdf'