{"parentUuid":"ecc01658-9de0-4fb0-898b-b71a38b88e4f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"6d252faa-d8a9-475a-b3d8-d0489bc8da88","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"floofy-puzzling-candle","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01JATYtXgcRqqV6ZMikqye2s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_016QDRZ33GKBiaMras5F28hc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/environment/skills/python-game-match-analysis.md","content":"# Game Match Analysis Pattern\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers common patterns for analyzing competitive game data where players compete against each other in matches, particularly when games need to be paired or compared.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Game vs Match\n- **Game**: A single instance of play (e.g., Game 1, Game 2, Game 3)\n- **Match**: A comparison or pairing of games (e.g., Game 1 vs Game 2)\n\n### Odd/Even Game Pairing\nCommon pattern: Odd-numbered games belong to Player 1, even-numbered games belong to Player 2.\n- Game 1 (Player 1) vs Game 2 (Player 2) = Match 1\n- Game 3 (Player 1) vs Game 4 (Player 2) = Match 2\n- Game 5 (Player 1) vs Game 6 (Player 2) = Match 3\n\n## Implementation Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Sequential Pairing\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Assuming df has columns: ['GameNumber', 'Score', 'Result']\n# where GameNumber starts from 1\n\ndef analyze_matches(df):\n    match_results = []\n\n    # Ensure data is sorted by game number\n    df = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Pair consecutive games\n    for i in range(0, len(df) - 1, 2):\n        game1 = df.iloc[i]      # Odd game (Player 1)\n        game2 = df.iloc[i + 1]  # Even game (Player 2)\n\n        # Determine winner\n        if game1['Score'] > game2['Score']:\n            winner = 'Player1'\n        elif game2['Score'] > game1['Score']:\n            winner = 'Player2'\n        else:\n            winner = 'Tie'\n\n        match_results.append({\n            'match_number': (i // 2) + 1,\n            'game1_number': game1['GameNumber'],\n            'game2_number': game2['GameNumber'],\n            'player1_score': game1['Score'],\n            'player2_score': game2['Score'],\n            'winner': winner\n        })\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(match_results)\n\n# Calculate wins\nresults_df = analyze_matches(df)\nplayer1_wins = len(results_df[results_df['winner'] == 'Player1'])\nplayer2_wins = len(results_df[results_df['winner'] == 'Player2'])\n\nprint(f\"Player 1 wins: {player1_wins}\")\nprint(f\"Player 2 wins: {player2_wins}\")\nprint(f\"Difference: {player1_wins - player2_wins}\")\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Filter Then Compare\n```python\ndef analyze_by_filtering(df):\n    # Separate odd and even games\n    odd_games = df[df['GameNumber'] % 2 == 1].sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n    even_games = df[df['GameNumber'] % 2 == 0].sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Ensure same length\n    min_len = min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))\n    odd_games = odd_games.iloc[:min_len]\n    even_games = even_games.iloc[:min_len]\n\n    player1_wins = 0\n    player2_wins = 0\n\n    for i in range(min_len):\n        p1_score = odd_games.iloc[i]['Score']\n        p2_score = even_games.iloc[i]['Score']\n\n        if p1_score > p2_score:\n            player1_wins += 1\n        elif p2_score > p1_score:\n            player2_wins += 1\n        # No increment for ties\n\n    return player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Vectorized Comparison\n```python\ndef vectorized_analysis(df):\n    # Separate and align\n    df_sorted = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Extract odd and even indexed rows (0-indexed)\n    odd_games = df_sorted.iloc[::2].reset_index(drop=True)\n    even_games = df_sorted.iloc[1::2].reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Ensure same length\n    min_len = min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))\n    odd_games = odd_games.iloc[:min_len]\n    even_games = even_games.iloc[:min_len]\n\n    # Vectorized comparison\n    player1_wins = (odd_games['Score'].values > even_games['Score'].values).sum()\n    player2_wins = (even_games['Score'].values > odd_games['Score'].values).sum()\n\n    return player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n## Handling Edge Cases\n\n### Unequal Number of Games\n```python\ndef safe_pairing(df):\n    \"\"\"Handle case where total games might be odd\"\"\"\n    total_games = len(df)\n\n    if total_games % 2 == 1:\n        print(f\"Warning: Odd number of games ({total_games}). Last game will be unpaired.\")\n        # Optionally remove last game\n        df = df.iloc[:-1]\n\n    return df\n```\n\n### Missing Game Numbers\n```python\ndef handle_missing_games(df):\n    \"\"\"Add game numbers if not present\"\"\"\n    if 'GameNumber' not in df.columns:\n        # Assign sequential game numbers starting from 1\n        df['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n    return df\n```\n\n### Non-sequential Game Numbers\n```python\ndef validate_game_sequence(df):\n    \"\"\"Check if games are properly numbered\"\"\"\n    expected = list(range(1, len(df) + 1))\n    actual = sorted(df['GameNumber'].tolist())\n\n    if expected != actual:\n        print(\"Warning: Game numbers are not sequential!\")\n        print(f\"Expected: {expected}\")\n        print(f\"Actual: {actual}\")\n        # Renumber games\n        df = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n        df['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n\n    return df\n```\n\n## Complete Example\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef complete_match_analysis(file_path):\n    \"\"\"\n    Complete analysis of matches between two players.\n\n    Assumes:\n    - Odd games (1, 3, 5, ...) are played by Player 1\n    - Even games (2, 4, 6, ...) are played by Player 2\n    - Games are paired: (1 vs 2), (3 vs 4), etc.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read data\n    df = pd.read_excel(file_path)\n\n    # Add game numbers if missing\n    if 'GameNumber' not in df.columns:\n        df['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n\n    # Sort by game number\n    df = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Handle odd total games\n    if len(df) % 2 == 1:\n        print(f\"Warning: {len(df)} total games. Excluding last game.\")\n        df = df.iloc[:-1]\n\n    # Initialize counters\n    player1_wins = 0\n    player2_wins = 0\n    ties = 0\n\n    # Pair and compare\n    for i in range(0, len(df), 2):\n        game1 = df.iloc[i]\n        game2 = df.iloc[i + 1]\n\n        # Determine winner based on score\n        if game1['Score'] > game2['Score']:\n            player1_wins += 1\n        elif game2['Score'] > game1['Score']:\n            player2_wins += 1\n        else:\n            ties += 1\n\n    # Calculate difference\n    difference = player1_wins - player2_wins\n\n    print(f\"Total matches: {len(df) // 2}\")\n    print(f\"Player 1 wins: {player1_wins}\")\n    print(f\"Player 2 wins: {player2_wins}\")\n    print(f\"Ties: {ties}\")\n    print(f\"Difference (P1 - P2): {difference}\")\n\n    return difference\n\n# Usage\nresult = complete_match_analysis('game_data.xlsx')\n```\n\n## Common Metrics\n\n### Win Percentage\n```python\ndef calculate_win_percentage(wins, total_matches):\n    return (wins / total_matches * 100) if total_matches > 0 else 0\n\nwin_pct_p1 = calculate_win_percentage(player1_wins, total_matches)\nwin_pct_p2 = calculate_win_percentage(player2_wins, total_matches)\n```\n\n### Head-to-Head Statistics\n```python\ndef detailed_stats(match_results_df):\n    stats = {\n        'total_matches': len(match_results_df),\n        'player1_wins': len(match_results_df[match_results_df['winner'] == 'Player1']),\n        'player2_wins': len(match_results_df[match_results_df['winner'] == 'Player2']),\n        'ties': len(match_results_df[match_results_df['winner'] == 'Tie']),\n        'avg_score_p1': match_results_df['player1_score'].mean(),\n        'avg_score_p2': match_results_df['player2_score'].mean(),\n    }\n    return stats\n```\n\n## Debugging Tips\n\n1. **Always verify game numbering:**\n   ```python\n   print(df['GameNumber'].tolist())\n   ```\n\n2. **Check pairing logic:**\n   ```python\n   for i in range(0, min(10, len(df)), 2):\n       print(f\"Match {i//2 + 1}: Game {df.iloc[i]['GameNumber']} vs Game {df.iloc[i+1]['GameNumber']}\")\n   ```\n\n3. **Validate data alignment:**\n   ```python\n   print(f\"Total games: {len(df)}\")\n   print(f\"Expected matches: {len(df) // 2}\")\n   ```\n\n## Best Practices\n1. Always sort data by game number before pairing\n2. Handle edge cases (odd number of games, missing data)\n3. Validate assumptions about data structure\n4. Use clear variable names (game1, game2, match_number)\n5. Add logging/printing for debugging\n6. Consider tie-breaking rules in your domain\n\n## Performance Considerations\n- For large datasets (>10,000 games), use vectorized operations\n- Avoid iterating when pandas operations can be used\n- Use `.values` for numpy array operations when possible\n- Reset index after filtering to avoid index misalignment\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2049,"cache_read_input_tokens":45211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2049,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":18}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbCTLLqHBatMYvMp5KPh","type":"assistant","uuid":"20c4593f-d987-424f-ac0a-37653f31607f","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:30:46.054Z"}
{"parentUuid":"20c4593f-d987-424f-ac0a-37653f31607f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"6d252faa-d8a9-475a-b3d8-d0489bc8da88","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"floofy-puzzling-candle","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_016QDRZ33GKBiaMras5F28hc","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/environment/skills/python-game-match-analysis.md"}]},"uuid":"00f45a8b-138a-4322-becf-c9a544dad091","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:30:46.093Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/root/environment/skills/python-game-match-analysis.md","content":"# Game Match Analysis Pattern\n\n## Overview\nThis skill covers common patterns for analyzing competitive game data where players compete against each other in matches, particularly when games need to be paired or compared.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Game vs Match\n- **Game**: A single instance of play (e.g., Game 1, Game 2, Game 3)\n- **Match**: A comparison or pairing of games (e.g., Game 1 vs Game 2)\n\n### Odd/Even Game Pairing\nCommon pattern: Odd-numbered games belong to Player 1, even-numbered games belong to Player 2.\n- Game 1 (Player 1) vs Game 2 (Player 2) = Match 1\n- Game 3 (Player 1) vs Game 4 (Player 2) = Match 2\n- Game 5 (Player 1) vs Game 6 (Player 2) = Match 3\n\n## Implementation Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Sequential Pairing\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Assuming df has columns: ['GameNumber', 'Score', 'Result']\n# where GameNumber starts from 1\n\ndef analyze_matches(df):\n    match_results = []\n\n    # Ensure data is sorted by game number\n    df = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Pair consecutive games\n    for i in range(0, len(df) - 1, 2):\n        game1 = df.iloc[i]      # Odd game (Player 1)\n        game2 = df.iloc[i + 1]  # Even game (Player 2)\n\n        # Determine winner\n        if game1['Score'] > game2['Score']:\n            winner = 'Player1'\n        elif game2['Score'] > game1['Score']:\n            winner = 'Player2'\n        else:\n            winner = 'Tie'\n\n        match_results.append({\n            'match_number': (i // 2) + 1,\n            'game1_number': game1['GameNumber'],\n            'game2_number': game2['GameNumber'],\n            'player1_score': game1['Score'],\n            'player2_score': game2['Score'],\n            'winner': winner\n        })\n\n    return pd.DataFrame(match_results)\n\n# Calculate wins\nresults_df = analyze_matches(df)\nplayer1_wins = len(results_df[results_df['winner'] == 'Player1'])\nplayer2_wins = len(results_df[results_df['winner'] == 'Player2'])\n\nprint(f\"Player 1 wins: {player1_wins}\")\nprint(f\"Player 2 wins: {player2_wins}\")\nprint(f\"Difference: {player1_wins - player2_wins}\")\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: Filter Then Compare\n```python\ndef analyze_by_filtering(df):\n    # Separate odd and even games\n    odd_games = df[df['GameNumber'] % 2 == 1].sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n    even_games = df[df['GameNumber'] % 2 == 0].sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Ensure same length\n    min_len = min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))\n    odd_games = odd_games.iloc[:min_len]\n    even_games = even_games.iloc[:min_len]\n\n    player1_wins = 0\n    player2_wins = 0\n\n    for i in range(min_len):\n        p1_score = odd_games.iloc[i]['Score']\n        p2_score = even_games.iloc[i]['Score']\n\n        if p1_score > p2_score:\n            player1_wins += 1\n        elif p2_score > p1_score:\n            player2_wins += 1\n        # No increment for ties\n\n    return player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Vectorized Comparison\n```python\ndef vectorized_analysis(df):\n    # Separate and align\n    df_sorted = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Extract odd and even indexed rows (0-indexed)\n    odd_games = df_sorted.iloc[::2].reset_index(drop=True)\n    even_games = df_sorted.iloc[1::2].reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Ensure same length\n    min_len = min(len(odd_games), len(even_games))\n    odd_games = odd_games.iloc[:min_len]\n    even_games = even_games.iloc[:min_len]\n\n    # Vectorized comparison\n    player1_wins = (odd_games['Score'].values > even_games['Score'].values).sum()\n    player2_wins = (even_games['Score'].values > odd_games['Score'].values).sum()\n\n    return player1_wins - player2_wins\n```\n\n## Handling Edge Cases\n\n### Unequal Number of Games\n```python\ndef safe_pairing(df):\n    \"\"\"Handle case where total games might be odd\"\"\"\n    total_games = len(df)\n\n    if total_games % 2 == 1:\n        print(f\"Warning: Odd number of games ({total_games}). Last game will be unpaired.\")\n        # Optionally remove last game\n        df = df.iloc[:-1]\n\n    return df\n```\n\n### Missing Game Numbers\n```python\ndef handle_missing_games(df):\n    \"\"\"Add game numbers if not present\"\"\"\n    if 'GameNumber' not in df.columns:\n        # Assign sequential game numbers starting from 1\n        df['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n    return df\n```\n\n### Non-sequential Game Numbers\n```python\ndef validate_game_sequence(df):\n    \"\"\"Check if games are properly numbered\"\"\"\n    expected = list(range(1, len(df) + 1))\n    actual = sorted(df['GameNumber'].tolist())\n\n    if expected != actual:\n        print(\"Warning: Game numbers are not sequential!\")\n        print(f\"Expected: {expected}\")\n        print(f\"Actual: {actual}\")\n        # Renumber games\n        df = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n        df['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n\n    return df\n```\n\n## Complete Example\n\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef complete_match_analysis(file_path):\n    \"\"\"\n    Complete analysis of matches between two players.\n\n    Assumes:\n    - Odd games (1, 3, 5, ...) are played by Player 1\n    - Even games (2, 4, 6, ...) are played by Player 2\n    - Games are paired: (1 vs 2), (3 vs 4), etc.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Read data\n    df = pd.read_excel(file_path)\n\n    # Add game numbers if missing\n    if 'GameNumber' not in df.columns:\n        df['GameNumber'] = range(1, len(df) + 1)\n\n    # Sort by game number\n    df = df.sort_values('GameNumber').reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    # Handle odd total games\n    if len(df) % 2 == 1:\n        print(f\"Warning: {len(df)} total games. Excluding last game.\")\n        df = df.iloc[:-1]\n\n    # Initialize counters\n    player1_wins = 0\n    player2_wins = 0\n    ties = 0\n\n    # Pair and compare\n    for i in range(0, len(df), 2):\n        game1 = df.iloc[i]\n        game2 = df.iloc[i + 1]\n\n        # Determine winner based on score\n        if game1['Score'] > game2['Score']:\n            player1_wins += 1\n        elif game2['Score'] > game1['Score']:\n            player2_wins += 1\n        else:\n            ties += 1\n\n    # Calculate difference\n    difference = player1_wins - player2_wins\n\n    print(f\"Total matches: {len(df) // 2}\")\n    print(f\"Player 1 wins: {player1_wins}\")\n    print(f\"Player 2 wins: {player2_wins}\")\n    print(f\"Ties: {ties}\")\n    print(f\"Difference (P1 - P2): {difference}\")\n\n    return difference\n\n# Usage\nresult = complete_match_analysis('game_data.xlsx')\n```\n\n## Common Metrics\n\n### Win Percentage\n```python\ndef calculate_win_percentage(wins, total_matches):\n    return (wins / total_matches * 100) if total_matches > 0 else 0\n\nwin_pct_p1 = calculate_win_percentage(player1_wins, total_matches)\nwin_pct_p2 = calculate_win_percentage(player2_wins, total_matches)\n```\n\n### Head-to-Head Statistics\n```python\ndef detailed_stats(match_results_df):\n    stats = {\n        'total_matches': len(match_results_df),\n        'player1_wins': len(match_results_df[match_results_df['winner'] == 'Player1']),\n        'player2_wins': len(match_results_df[match_results_df['winner'] == 'Player2']),\n        'ties': len(match_results_df[match_results_df['winner'] == 'Tie']),\n        'avg_score_p1': match_results_df['player1_score'].mean(),\n        'avg_score_p2': match_results_df['player2_score'].mean(),\n    }\n    return stats\n```\n\n## Debugging Tips\n\n1. **Always verify game numbering:**\n   ```python\n   print(df['GameNumber'].tolist())\n   ```\n\n2. **Check pairing logic:**\n   ```python\n   for i in range(0, min(10, len(df)), 2):\n       print(f\"Match {i//2 + 1}: Game {df.iloc[i]['GameNumber']} vs Game {df.iloc[i+1]['GameNumber']}\")\n   ```\n\n3. **Validate data alignment:**\n   ```python\n   print(f\"Total games: {len(df)}\")\n   print(f\"Expected matches: {len(df) // 2}\")\n   ```\n\n## Best Practices\n1. Always sort data by game number before pairing\n2. Handle edge cases (odd number of games, missing data)\n3. Validate assumptions about data structure\n4. Use clear variable names (game1, game2, match_number)\n5. Add logging/printing for debugging\n6. Consider tie-breaking rules in your domain\n\n## Performance Considerations\n- For large datasets (>10,000 games), use vectorized operations\n- Avoid iterating when pandas operations can be used\n- Use `.values` for numpy array operations when possible\n- Reset index after filtering to avoid index misalignment\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"20c4593f-d987-424f-ac0a-37653f31607f"}
